---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import FAQPageSchema from '../components/FAQPageSchema.astro';
import LocalBusinessSchema from '../components/LocalBusinessSchema.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';

const city = "Scotch Plains";
const latitude = 40.5578;
const longitude = -74.3629;

const faqs = [
  { q: "How far is AllStar from Scotch Plains?", a: "About 12 minutes via Route 22. 1166 West Chestnut St, Union. Free parking on-site." },
  { q: "What programs are available?", a: "Adult BJJ, Muay Thai, and MMA (ages 16+). Kids Lions (7–13) and Cubs (4–6). Summer camp runs seasonally." },
  { q: "Do I need experience?", a: "No. Most students — adults and kids — start with none." },
  { q: "Can I watch a class before enrolling my child?", a: "Yes. Walk in any time. We don't hide what we do." },
  { q: "What's the free trial?", a: "Two weeks of unlimited classes. Adults can try any program. Kids can try their age group. No card required, no contract, no pressure." },
  { q: "How do I start?", a: "Fill out the form on this page or call (908) 341-1131. We'll text to confirm a class time." },
];
---

<PageLayout
  title="Martial Arts in Scotch Plains, NJ — BJJ, Muay Thai & Kids Classes | AllStar"
  description="Martial arts classes for Scotch Plains, NJ families at AllStar Martial Arts in Union. BJJ, Muay Thai, MMA, and Kids programs. Renzo Gracie black belt. Free 2-week trial."
  ogImage="/images/adult-bjj-hero.jpg"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <LocalBusinessSchema city={city} latitude={latitude} longitude={longitude} />
    <FAQPageSchema faqs={faqs} />
  </Fragment>

  <PageHero
    eyebrow="12 minutes from Scotch Plains"
    headline="Martial Arts in Scotch Plains, NJ"
    sub="Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu, Muay Thai, MMA, and kids classes — a 12-minute run east on Route 22 to Union. Free 2-week trial, no contract."
    bgImage="/images/adult-bjj-hero.jpg"
  />

  <!-- Intro -->
  <section class="section-pad bg-white">
    <div class="container-page max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-brand-gray leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Scotch Plains sits on the quieter, leafier side of Route 22, and AllStar is about 12 minutes east on that same highway — from the downtown by the Fanwood border straight to our facility at 1166 West Chestnut in Union. Free parking on-site, so the trip ends the moment you pull in. Families weighing us against gyms toward <a href="/westfield/" class="text-brand-navy font-bold hover:text-brand-gold transition-colors">Westfield</a> or <a href="/mountainside/" class="text-brand-navy font-bold hover:text-brand-gold transition-colors">Mountainside</a> usually decide on what happens once they're on the mat.
      </p>
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">
        And what happens on the mat comes down to the coach. Jamal Patterson is a Renzo Gracie black belt, ADCC veteran, and former professional MMA fighter who competed in the IFL and Bellator. That competition pedigree changes how technique gets taught — the detail, the pressure, the why. Students five and ten years deep will tell you the difference is obvious.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BJJ -->
  <section class="section-pad bg-brand-gray-light">
    <div class="container-page max-w-3xl">
      <div class="eyebrow">Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu</div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl text-brand-black mb-5">BJJ Classes Near Scotch Plains, NJ</h2>
      <p class="text-brand-gray leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu is our flagship program. Adults 16 and up, and beginners are the rule — most students walk in having never touched a gi. Want specifics before you visit? Our <a href="/adult-bjj/" class="text-brand-navy font-bold hover:text-brand-gold transition-colors">adult BJJ program</a> spells it out.
      </p>
      <p class="text-brand-gray leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Plenty of schools around here teach BJJ, and a few even share our lineage. The difference is the coach. Jamal's resume — ADCC, IFL, Bellator, UWC champion — isn't a poster on the wall; it lives in every technique he drills with the room.
      </p>
      <p class="text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">
        Evening classes at 6, 7, and 8 PM most weekdays, built around commuters and working adults who don't get home until after six. Two weeks free. No contract.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Kids -->
  <section class="section-pad bg-white">
    <div class="container-page max-w-3xl">
      <div class="eyebrow">Kids Martial Arts</div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl text-brand-black mb-5">Kids Martial Arts Near Scotch Plains, NJ</h2>
      <div class="space-y-5">
        <div class="bg-brand-gray-light p-6 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-brand-gold">
          <h3 class="text-xl text-brand-black mb-2">Cubs — Ages 4–6</h3>
          <p class="text-brand-gray text-sm leading-relaxed">Preschool-age energy with martial arts structure. Focus on coordination, listening, and confidence. Short activities, high engagement, constant positive reinforcement.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-brand-gray-light p-6 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-brand-navy">
          <h3 class="text-xl text-brand-black mb-2">Lions — Ages 7–13</h3>
          <p class="text-brand-gray text-sm leading-relaxed">Real Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu technique. Takedowns, escapes, positions. These kids are not doing karate katas — they're learning a system that works. Parents consistently report that the confidence carries into school.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-brand-gray leading-relaxed mt-5">
        Bully prevention is a genuine part of what Scotch Plains parents get here. When a kid actually knows they can handle themselves, the dynamic with a bully shifts without a single punch being thrown — see how we approach it on our <a href="/self-defense/" class="text-brand-navy font-bold hover:text-brand-gold transition-colors">self-defense page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Muay Thai + MMA -->
  <section class="section-pad bg-brand-navy text-white">
    <div class="container-page max-w-4xl">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow text-brand-gold">Muay Thai</div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-4">Muay Thai Near Scotch Plains, NJ</h2>
          <p class="text-white/90 leading-relaxed">
            This is the one nobody else in central Union County offers. Across the Scotch Plains, Fanwood, and Union area, you won't find authentic Muay Thai taught next to real BJJ — genuine pad work, technique, and conditioning. Beginners are welcome from the first round.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow text-brand-gold">MMA</div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-4">MMA Classes Near Scotch Plains, NJ</h2>
          <p class="text-white/90 leading-relaxed">
            Our MMA program puts BJJ, Muay Thai, and wrestling together into one complete system, coached by Jamal Patterson — a pro MMA fighter who has cornered UFC athletes from their amateur debut to the pros. Adults 16 and up.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Landmarks -->
  <section class="section-pad bg-white">
    <div class="container-page max-w-3xl">
      <div class="eyebrow">If you know Scotch Plains</div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl text-brand-black mb-5">You Know These Spots — We're 12 Minutes Away</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        {["Downtown Scotch Plains", "Scotch Plains Public Library", "Fanwood border", "Route 22 corridor", "Green Brook Park", "Scotch Plains High School", "Park Middle School", "Scotch Plains Municipal Pool"].map((l) => (
          <span class="bg-brand-gray-light text-brand-gray px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm">📍 {l}</span>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FAQ items={faqs} />

  <CTA
    headline="Two Weeks Free — Scotch Plains Families Welcome"
    sub="Show up. Bring water. We'll handle the rest. No commitment, no pressure."
  />
</PageLayout>
